The city shall have 30 days to investigate the application and the background of the applicant from the date on which the applicant appears and submits his application and required fee, as described in Section 10-184. Upon completion of the investigation, the mayor and city commission may issue the license if it finds:
(1) The required fee has been paid;
(2) The application conforms in all respects to the provisions of this article;
(3) The applicant has not knowingly made a material misrepresentation in the application;
(4) The applicant has fully cooperated in the investigation of his application;
(5) The applicant, if an individual, or any of the stockholders of the corporation, any officers or directors, if the applicant is a corporation, or any of the partners, including limited partners, if the applicant is a partnership, has not been convicted in a court of competent jurisdiction of an offense involving dishonesty, fraud, deceit, or moral turpitude, convicted of an attempt to commit any such offenses, or convicted in any state of any offense which, if committed or attempted in this state, would have been punishable as a crime involving dishonesty, fraud, deceit or moral turpitude;
(6) The applicant has not had a sexually oriented business license or other similar license or permit denied or revoked for cause by this city or any other city located in or out of this state prior to the date of application;
(7) The building, structure, equipment or location of such business, if used, as proposed by the applicant, would comply with all applicable laws, including, but not limited to, health, zoning, distance, fire and safety requirements and standards;
(8) The applicant is at least 21 years of age;
(9) That the applicant, his or her employee, agent, partner, director, officer, stockholder or manager has not, within five years of the date of the application, knowingly allowed or permitted any of the specified sexual activities as defined herein to be committed or allowed in or upon the premises where such adult entertainment establishment is to be located or to be used as a place in which solicitations for the specified sexual activities as defined herein openly occur;
(10) That on the date the business for which a permit is required herein commences, and thereafter, there will be a responsible person on the premises to act as manager at all times during which the business is open;
(11) That the proposed premises is not to be located too close, as defined in this article, to any church, synagogue, mosque, or other place of worship, school, library, governmental building or site or any other business restricted hereunder;
(12) That the grant of such license will not cause a violation of this article or any other ordinance or regulation of the city, the state or the United States;
(13) That the applicant is not delinquent in the payment to the City of taxes, fees, fines, or penalties assessed against or imposed upon the applicant in relation to any business operated by the applicant within the City of Toccoa;
(14) That the applicant has not been convicted of a specified criminal activity, felony, or other crime of moral turpitude. The fact that a conviction is being appealed should have no effect under this subsection. For the purpose of this subsection, the term "conviction" means a conviction, guilty plea, or plea of nolo contendere and includes a conviction of any business entity for which the applicant had, at the time of the offense leading to the conviction for specified criminal activity, a management responsibility or a controlling ownership interest;
(15) That the proposed sexually oriented business is not located in a zoning district other than a district in which sexually oriented businesses are allowed to operate under this or the city's zoning ordinances; and,
(16) That the person making the application is not prohibited, as a licensee, pursuant to section 10-185 of this article.
(Ord. No. 2006-19, § 1, 11-13-06)

